{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["לחם פנים — according to its plain sense: bread fitting to be set before dignitaries, fine bread, as written: ולקחת סלת ואפית אותה וגו׳. And written: וישא משאת מאת פניו אליהם. And written: ולחנה יתן מנה אחת אפים — a choice portion from the bowl of importance set before Elkana, for the ones they set before the head of the household; כי את חנה אהב — therefore אפים, distinguished. And HaShem had closed her womb — therefore one מנה and not two and not many portions as for Peninnah, who had sons and daughters."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The lemma and scriptural quotations are rendered in Hebrew script per instructions; the quotation ולקחת סלת ואפית אותה וגו׳ is from 1 Samuel, not Exodus."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:05.443487470Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}